Falsifies `byte_glob::verification::star_matches_anything_and_question_matches_one_byte`.

The defect: once the name is spent, the matcher skips `?` as well as `*`, so `?` matches the empty name.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(matches_with(b"?", n, LeadingDot::Ordinary), nlen == 1)` at `nlen == 0`.

diff --git a/src/lib.rs b/src/lib.rs
--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -176,7 +176,7 @@
             // The name is spent. Nothing can be gained by backtracking, since that only makes the
             // `*` absorb more of a name that has no more bytes, so the answer is fixed: whatever is
             // left of the pattern has to be able to match emptiness, and only `*` can.
-            while pattern.get(j) == Some(&b'*') {
+            while matches!(pattern.get(j), Some(&b'*') | Some(&b'?')) {
                 j += 1;
                 steps += 1;
             }
